{
  "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/parental-responsibility",
  "type": "Concept",
  "prefLabel": {
    "en": "parental responsibility"
  },
  "definition": {
    "en": "The set of duties and powers of those who care for, raise, educate, represent and protect a child, always exercised in the child's interest and with respect for the child's evolving capacities."
  },
  "scopeNote": {
    "en": [
      "It is a function oriented towards the child's well-being, not a power over the child; in some legal systems it takes the form of national institutions such as parental authority. Where the parents have a disability, it also includes the right to receive appropriate assistance in carrying out their child-rearing responsibilities, as well as the prohibition on separating a child from their parents on the ground of disability."
    ]
  },
  "notation": [
    "2.5"
  ],
